  "source": "Novus N1020 communication protocol V10x A",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "N1020 Communication Protocol",
      "version": "V10x A",
      "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/35246212/doc.pdf",
      "note": "tables 2 and 3 and the register table",
      "accessed": "2026-11-26",
      "sha256": "c0430c5395f12c8c384d4380609773afdd55744a59ac7b9f308b54e07b954a45"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface. Functions 03, 05, 06 and 16; broadcast (address 0) writes only.",
    "8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no, even or odd parity and 1200 to 115200 bit/s. The document gives no factory address, baud rate or parity: check the controller; 9600 bit/s without parity is assumed here.",
    "The process value, setpoints and alarm values are integers in the display unit, with the decimal places of register 30; a temperature is read multiplied by 10.",
    "A write outside the allowed range stores the nearest limit and returns it.",
    "The document says only registers above address 12 can be written, but marks some of those below as writable; the descriptions of each register are followed.",
    "The document prints 32400 for baud rate value 5, while its list of speeds has 38400; 38400 is used here.",
    "The document lists the output states as coils 0 to 4 although the status words show two outputs.",
    "Reserved and internal registers are left out. Written from the manufacturer's document; not tested on a device."
  ],
